# RP6 slimming fragment, merged by scripts/10-build-kernel.sh after defconfig
# and before the DT-derived symbols (dt.config) and kernel/rp6.config, so
# anything the device tree or rp6.config asks for wins over what is dropped
# here. Qualcomm clock, pinctrl and interconnect drivers for other SoCs are
# dropped by a generated fragment (soc.config) in the build script.
#
# Kept on purpose: USB-C peripherals a handheld gets plugged into (USB audio,
# HID, USB Ethernet adapters, mass storage, gadget mode for debugging),
# Bluetooth HID, netfilter/NAT for Waydroid, FUSE and overlayfs.

# --- Firmware interfaces: OpenABL boots with a device tree ---
# CONFIG_ACPI is not set
# CONFIG_GOOGLE_FIRMWARE is not set
# CONFIG_CHROME_PLATFORMS is not set
